# Line-ending policy (I-07 / E-12).
#
# Without this file a Windows checkout with `core.autocrlf=true` writes CRLF into
# the working tree and Git prints "LF will be replaced by CRLF" on every `git add`
# — a per-machine setting leaking into every contributor's diffs. `text=auto`
# normalizes line endings to LF in the repository (the single canonical form) and
# `eol=lf` keeps them LF in the working tree on every platform, so the files in
# the repository, in the working tree and in `git diff` are byte-identical.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Machine-written runtime artifacts (tailing logs, model caches, downloaded media)
# are never edited by hand and must never be re-encoded on their way in or out.
data/** -text
runtime/** -text
logs/** -text
